VodSync imports MediaBunny's container readers and browser media APIs. The production build transforms and tree-shakes unmodified installed MediaBunny modules into the audio synchronization worker JavaScript. That transformed portion remains Covered Software under MPL-2.0; it is not covered by VodSync's Apache-2.0 licence.

No MediaBunny source file is edited, patched, or replaced by this project. Build-time bundling and minification transform the unmodified package for browser delivery, but the project does not maintain a modified MediaBunny source fork.

### Corresponding source availability

The official npm archive at `third_party/mediabunny-1.50.8.tgz` is retained for exact build provenance. It contains the published `src/`, `dist/`, `LICENSE`, `README.md`, and package metadata, but it omits four upstream `shared/` TypeScript source files represented in its compiled modules. It is therefore not treated as complete corresponding source by itself.

The corresponding-source archive at `third_party/mediabunny-1.50.8-corresponding-source.tar.gz` combines the exact npm `src/` tree with all five files from upstream commit `db75747533958f4a9c81d6510d02a2c9de708c04` under `shared/`, including `aac-misc.ts`, `ac3-misc.ts`, `bitstream.ts`, `mp3-misc.ts`, and `tsconfig.json`. It also includes the unmodified MPL-2.0 licence, package metadata, README, and TypeScript configuration. No MediaBunny source file was changed. The source is available at no charge both in this repository and beside the deployed executable.

